(270170, 16783, 6870, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I concur with all of the compliments below! Including my own! <br/> <br/>This is a superb shot with a difficult subject, but here is why I think it works so well:<br/> <br/>It is simple, and you suggest a lot. The way the numbers vanish indicate the infinitity of pi, and your use of B/W is appropriate and adds interest. Your point of view, with the numbers tilting off, enhance the interest as well. The cleanliness of line and contrast of B/W create a suggestion of mystery as well, taking our thoughts beyond the photo and into the realms of mathematics and their incomprehensibleness, yet seeming simplicity. Again, the simplicity of the image is both appropriate and ironic.<br/> <br/>What can I say? This is a marvelous shot. Star sending it to math textbook companies!<br/> <br/>Thanks,<br/> <br/>David</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I concur with all of the compliments below! Including my own!  This is a superb shot with a difficult subject, but here is why I think it works so well: It is simple, and you suggest a lot. The way the numbers vanish indicate the infinitity of pi, and your use of B/W is appropriate and adds interest. Your point of view, with the numbers tilting off, enhance the interest as well. The cleanliness of line and contrast of B/W create a suggestion of mystery as well, taking our thoughts beyond the photo and into the realms of mathematics and their incomprehensibleness, yet seeming simplicity. Again, the simplicity of the image is both appropriate and ironic. What can I say? This is a marvelous shot. Star sending it to math textbook companies! Thanks, David', '2003-04-18 11:03:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(270286, 17347, 4493, '<td valign="top">Critique Club Comment:<br/> <br/>The negative space and warm feel of this shot is very nice. I think that as far as meeting the challenge goes, it does so as well. This shots only negative that I really can comment on is that the focus seems soft. I don''t know if it''s because you need to do a sharpen after resizing to this size, or if it''s because the actual focus was off. The lighting is well done and I imagine keeping stray reflections from showing up on the glass was no easy task.<br/> <br/>Your shot is nice. It has an old world feel to it.</td>', 'Critique Club Comment: The negative space and warm feel of this shot is very nice. I think that as far as meeting the challenge goes, it does so as well. This shots only negative that I really can comment on is that the focus seems soft. I don''t know if it''s because you need to do a sharpen after resizing to this size, or if it''s because the actual focus was off. The lighting is well done and I imagine keeping stray reflections from showing up on the glass was no easy task. Your shot is nice. It has an old world feel to it.', '2003-04-18 12:55:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(270402, 17396, 6870, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>This is a nice image addressin the pi challenge. I concur with all of the compliments below! <br/> <br/>I like the scientific tone this photo, created with the calculations and instruments, as well as the excellent lighting. I mentioned below that I thought the yellow tape measure took away from this slightly, perhaps because the tape measure is not a very accurate instrument relative to pi or the other objects selected for your photo.<br/> <br/>As someone else noted, the arrangement is loose, perhaps a tighter arrangement with a closer point of view would enhance the feeling of precision and intricacy. I hope you realize that these suggestions can come because it is a strong image already. The composition and focus are superb, and the little touches like the tape going around the round object make this an intriguing and engaging image to begin with.<br/> <br/>The lighting is also appropriately cool and scientific. I like how the calculations were done in a fine point pen.<br/> <br/>I look forward to seeing more of  your work! Good luck!<br/> <br/>-David</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! This is a nice image addressin the pi challenge. I concur with all of the compliments below!  I like the scientific tone this photo, created with the calculations and instruments, as well as the excellent lighting. I mentioned below that I thought the yellow tape measure took away from this slightly, perhaps because the tape measure is not a very accurate instrument relative to pi or the other objects selected for your photo. As someone else noted, the arrangement is loose, perhaps a tighter arrangement with a closer point of view would enhance the feeling of precision and intricacy. I hope you realize that these suggestions can come because it is a strong image already. The composition and focus are superb, and the little touches like the tape going around the round object make this an intriguing and engaging image to begin with. The lighting is also appropriately cool and scientific. I like how the calculations were done in a fine point pen. I look forward to seeing more of  your work! Good luck! -David', '2003-04-18 15:32:07.000000', NULL, 0),
